{
 "_doc": "API -> IPC mapping, the missing middle of the MCP -> API -> IPC chain (the MCP -> API half is data/mcp-catalogue.json, generated). Hand-declared from the real dispatch in server/src (each route's `via` names the code path). `ipc` is null (pure HTTP, no IPC leg), \"unmapped\" (link not determinable from the code) or a list of ipc_endpoints ids. Surfaces: app = ROUTES in app.rs (loopback :8002, /__app__), mesh = the mesh listener (meshlogs.rs, routes from build.json::mesh), diag = the :8003 listener (lib.rs handle_diag). Every ROUTES row MUST appear here (test: api_ipc_map_covers_every_route). `mcp_tools` links a catalogue tool to a webserver route (meshlogs.rs: /endpoints is 'for cloudy-c3-mcp'; basis is the phone_* tool names); the catalogue itself carries no such link.",
 "surfaces": {
  "app": {
   "listener": "loopback :8002 /__app__",
   "auth": "loopback + allowed host; POST needs x-c3-write and application/json"
  },
  "mesh": {
   "listener": "mesh address (build.json::mesh)",
   "auth": "Bearer fleet token + mesh peers only"
  },
  "diag": {
   "listener": "loopback :8003",
   "auth": "loopback + allowed host"
  }
 },
 "ipc_endpoints": [
  {
   "id": "logexport",
   "kind": "provider",
   "template": "build.json::api.ipc#logexport",
   "what": "per-app log export provider"
  },
  {
   "id": "fleet",
   "kind": "provider",
   "template": "build.json::api.ipc#fleet",
   "what": "per-app fleet handshake; the mesh bearer token is read through it"
  },
  {
   "id": "headless",
   "kind": "provider",
   "authority_mesh": [
    "browser_package",
    "browser_suffix"
   ],
   "what": "Cloud-Browser headless provider (build.json::mesh)"
  },
  {
   "id": "shellbroker",
   "kind": "provider",
   "authority_mesh": [
    "shell_package",
    "shell_suffix"
   ],
   "what": "SuperApp shell broker provider (build.json::mesh)"
  },
  {
   "id": "fleetdiag",
   "kind": "provider",
   "authority": "<superapp>.fleetdiag",
   "what": "SuperApp FleetDiagnosticsProvider (diag.rs set_source)"
  },
  {
   "id": "browser-open",
   "kind": "intent",
   "authority": null,
   "what": "Intent handing an http(s) URL to cloud-browser (diag.rs set_opener)"
  },
  {
   "id": "nix-door",
   "kind": "intent",
   "authority": null,
   "what": "Intent to the nix app's service starting/stopping the supervised SSH door (door.rs set_sender)"
  },
  {
   "id": "app-launch",
   "kind": "intent",
   "authority": null,
   "what": "Launch activity of a terminal app's package (served.rs set_launcher)"
  }
 ],
